{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Bookings tracks arrangements made on behalf of guests: private transfers,
        taxis, restaurant reservations, tours, spa appointments, tickets, and
        anything else the desk organises. It is not the room reservation system;
        it's the concierge's ledger.
    </p>

    <h2>How a booking moves</h2>
    <p>
        Each booking has a status: <strong>unconfirmed</strong> when it's first
        logged, <strong>confirmed</strong> once the supplier has agreed,
        <strong>completed</strong> after it happens, or <strong>cancelled</strong>.
        Open bookings whose date has passed are flagged on the dashboard as
        needing attention.
    </p>

    <h2>Common tasks</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>Open <strong>General → Bookings</strong> to see the hotel's bookings.</li>
        <li>Create a booking with the guest's details, the type, and the date.</li>
        <li>Update the status as the arrangement progresses; every change is recorded in the booking's log.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="au-docs-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info"></i>
        <p>
            Editing and deleting bookings requires manage permission on the
            module. Deleting is permanent, so prefer cancelling.
        </p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
